From ff4dd9d0d87d6a6380c807303470144b75901e49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:54:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Match app visual identity to TrustMate Marketplace
 (Grab20/TrustMate)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pulled the actual design tokens from the Marketplace's source (globals.css,
homepage, cars/driver listing pages) and repointed the driver app's palette
to match exactly: primary green #1A2E1A, accent green #1A5C28, cream page
background #FAFAF8, ink #0D1F0E, secondary grey #666, plus the Marketplace's
pending/error status colors. The Marketplace has no gold or teal anywhere,
so those tokens now render as greens (a bright accent for highlights on
dark cards, a pale pill background for light-surface badges) rather than
being retired outright, since ~20 files reference them for the same visual
role the Marketplace fills with its light-green pill/badge treatment.

Existing token names were kept as-is and only their values changed, so
every call site picks up the new palette without needing individual edits
— this repo already used that alias pattern for an earlier rebrand pass.

Also added PT Serif (bundled, since Georgia isn't available on Android) for
heading-shaped MD3 variants (display/headline/title), matching the
Marketplace's Georgia-serif-headings + sans-serif-body pairing, while body
and label text stay on the platform sans-serif default.
